#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_wavelet_packet_transform

#% text
# `discrete_wavelet_packet_transform(data)`, `(data, w)`, `(data, w, r)` give the wavelet packet transform: as `discrete_wavelet_transform`, but every node of the tree, details included, is split again at the next level.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
d = discrete_wavelet_packet_transform(n(range(8)), haar_wavelet(), 2)

#% cell
map(r => r[1], d(automatic))
#% output
#= [[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]]

#% cell
chop(inverse_wavelet_transform(d) - range(8))
#% output
#= [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]

